    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<h3>Mindrot</h3><p><em>[Curse][Magical][Occult][Mental]</em></p><p>A deadly curse that causes a creature to entirely lose their ability to think, eventually reducing them to a mindless, puppetlike husk.</p><div data-visibility=\"gm\"><p><strong>Special </strong>The effective level of this curse is equal to the APL of the party.</p><p><strong>Saving Throw </strong>@Check[will|dc:0|options:curse,magical,occult,mental] ( <strong>#DC#</strong> for APL)</p><p><strong>Effect </strong>The afflicted creature has a -1 untyped penalty to saves against mental affects, increasing per stage of the affliction to a maximum of 10. At stage 10, the creature loses the ability to think entirely, becoming a mindless husk that is considered dead (though the body technically remains living).</p></div>"
